1
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:11,967
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:23,300
<i>Gandang Gabi, Kapamilya
and   Kapuso!</i>

3
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:25,200
Yes!

4
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:33,667
Are you happy that we're all
ending the week together?!

5
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,900
Yes!

6
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:40,833
We can't end the week
without having fun, right?

7
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:41,833
[TETAY] Right!

8
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,600
That is why we are here again
to have--

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,467
Let me see your smiles.
Yes, that's it.

10
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:50,700
We'll end the week with a bang
because, my God!

11
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,767
What date is it?

12
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:55,867
What date is it?

13
00:00:55,867 --> 00:00:59,200
2026 isn't slowing down because
it's already the Ber months.

14
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,900
But, hey, be honest.
You like it, don't you?

15
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:06,433
You like
those Christmas feels, right?

16
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:07,600
[TETAY] Yes!

17
00:01:07,633 --> 00:01:09,867
[VICE] Do you feel
the Christmas feels?

18
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,400
- [AUDIENCE] Yes!
- [VICE] My God,

19
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,733
mornings are so cold now,

20
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:15,600
especially when you don't
have hot water, right?

21
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:18,533
I can't imagine a Christmas
without caroling.

22
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:21,900
- That's sad, right?
- [AUDIENCE] Yes!

23
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,033
Geng Gang, come here.

24
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:27,267
- Verna, Vince, and Tetay.
- Hi, Meme!

25
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:29,033
Okay.

26
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,667
We're all right, Verna!

27
00:01:33,233 --> 00:01:36,833
My God. I know it's Vince
you want to kiss.

28
00:01:36,833 --> 00:01:38,700
- Okay.
- I've done that earlier.

29
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:42,167
Did you go caroling
when you were a kid?

30
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,433
Yes, I did.

31
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:47,433
Really? Like, regularly,
every Christmas season?

32
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:49,100
- Yes, Meme.
- What's the biggest amount

33
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,367
you've received?

34
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:55,567
For the whole December,
I gathered around 10,000 pesos.

35
00:01:55,567 --> 00:01:57,167
- [AUDIENCE] Wow!
- Wow!

36
00:01:57,167 --> 00:02:00,667
- Really, "gather"?
- She really said "gather."

37
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:02,533
I was alone
when I went caroling.

38
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:04,467
But 10,000?
Where did you go caroling?

39
00:02:04,467 --> 00:02:05,967
They paid you well.

40
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:08,167
Caroling is different from
breaking into someone's house.

41
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:13,000
No, I went caroling as early
as the first week of December,

42
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,333
so I could save money
for Christmas dinner.

43
00:02:15,367 --> 00:02:18,700
- 10,000 seems like a joke.
- It's not! It's real!

44
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,067
Sometimes, I get 2000 pesos
for one night.

45
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:22,800
I was alone, I had no one
to share it with.

46
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:25,867
Even so. How much does
one family give you?

47
00:02:25,867 --> 00:02:27,800
Well, I sing one whole album.

48
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,267
- That's why they pay a lot.
- [LAUGHING SFX]

49
00:02:29,267 --> 00:02:30,300
[VICE] This woman, really.

50
00:02:30,833 --> 00:02:32,933
Did you go caroling
when you were a kid?

51
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:34,867
- No, back in the States--
- Oh, but he's rich.

52
00:02:34,867 --> 00:02:36,267
He's from Valle Verde.

53
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:38,800
[TETAY]
And in the States, too, when--

54
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:42,100
States? You don't even have
a passport.

55
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:45,767
No, but we also went caroling
before in San Juan.

56
00:02:45,767 --> 00:02:48,333
How much does one family
give you?

57
00:02:48,367 --> 00:02:51,500
I think a maximum of 500 pesos
for one night.

58
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,133
- Then we save it.
- [VICE] Yes.

59
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:56,733
- 50 pesos is already a lot.
- It is.

60
00:02:56,733 --> 00:02:59,100
During my time, they gave us
chump change.

61
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,500
- Yes.
- Right?

62
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,700
When you're an actual choir
and you give an envelope,

63
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:04,633
that's when they pay you a lot.

64
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,233
[TETAY] What about Vince?

65
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:09,367
That's why I asked him last
'cause he's rich.

66
00:03:09,367 --> 00:03:12,000
How do you go caroling
in villages?

67
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,500
In our village,
it's the church choir

68
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,967
- that goes caroling.
- [VERNA] Wow!

69
00:03:17,967 --> 00:03:22,433
I never experienced
caroling myself.

70
00:03:22,467 --> 00:03:24,667
When you were a kid, you and
your friends never experienced

71
00:03:24,667 --> 00:03:26,400
knocking on doors,
and caroling?

72
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,967
- [TETAY] Or ding dong ditch?
- No.

73
00:03:27,967 --> 00:03:31,600
Usually, during Christmas break,
we do our own stuff.

74
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,767
That's what I experienced.

75
00:03:32,767 --> 00:03:34,767
[VICE] Like, your other
neighbors are in Europe.

76
00:03:34,767 --> 00:03:36,633
- [TETAY] And what did we do?
- Yes.

77
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:39,400
The nearest one's probably
in Hong Kong.

78
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,967
But us, we really went
door-to-door.

79
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:44,867
But I also feel like the kids
don't go caroling nowadays.

80
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:46,633
But it's nice
if it were still a thing, right?

81
00:03:46,633 --> 00:03:48,333
Yeah, but they've evolved now.

82
00:03:48,333 --> 00:03:50,767
Others who go caroling now

83
00:03:50,767 --> 00:03:54,033
bring a bluetooth speaker
with them.

84
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,333
- Yes.
- Yes, it's evolved now.

85
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:58,633
They use a QR code
to ask for money.

86
00:03:58,633 --> 00:04:00,200
[VINCE CHUCKLING]

87
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,867
- There's no more cash?
- [VINCE] None.

88
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,633
It is no longer on a cash basis.

89
00:04:03,633 --> 00:04:05,033
- They use QR codes now.
- It's cashless.

90
00:04:05,033 --> 00:04:07,533
- Cashless caroling.
- You just scan it.

91
00:04:07,533 --> 00:04:08,800
Bar code.

92
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,200
In the history
of the Philippines,

93
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:15,133
caroling is one of the earliest
forms of scam.

94
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:18,033
I mean, we don't all
sing well, right?

95
00:04:18,033 --> 00:04:19,233
But we go caroling either way,

96
00:04:19,233 --> 00:04:21,800
and we're even mad
if we don't receive money.

97
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,200
[SINGING]
<i> Thank you, thank you</i>

98
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,533
<i>Ang babarat ninyo
(You're so stingy)</i>

99
00:04:24,533 --> 00:04:26,167
Then we'll run away.

100
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:28,400
Or if they tell us,

101
00:04:28,433 --> 00:04:30,267
"Sorry. Just come back
on Christmas,"

102
00:04:30,267 --> 00:04:32,700
