I listened to her side,

966
00:43:19,867 --> 00:43:22,367
where she was coming from,
and where I was coming from.

967
00:43:22,367 --> 00:43:24,467
Because after all,
we were just tired.

968
00:43:24,500 --> 00:43:26,767
We only said those things
because we were tired.

969
00:43:26,767 --> 00:43:27,833
Besides, it's impossible
for a group

970
00:43:27,833 --> 00:43:29,500
to exist without
anyone fighting.

971
00:43:29,500 --> 00:43:31,300
- There are disagreements.
- Yes, yes.

972
00:43:31,300 --> 00:43:34,400
It's ideal to think that
everyone will always get along.

973
00:43:34,400 --> 00:43:36,167
It's possible,

974
00:43:36,167 --> 00:43:41,067
but there will be times when you
just won't see eye to eye.

975
00:43:41,067 --> 00:43:42,433
That's normal.

976
00:43:42,433 --> 00:43:44,967
It doesn't mean
your group is weak.

977
00:43:44,967 --> 00:43:47,267
Sometimes, there are
misunderstandings.

978
00:43:47,267 --> 00:43:49,567
People get on each
other's nerves.

979
00:43:49,567 --> 00:43:51,733
That happens in any group.

980
00:43:51,733 --> 00:43:53,500
Are you guys close?

981
00:43:53,500 --> 00:43:54,900
- Yes.
- Yes.

982
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:56,900
[ARIANNE] It's just not obvious.

983
00:43:56,933 --> 00:43:58,500
Like, are you really
close friends?

984
00:43:58,500 --> 00:44:01,300
Do you still hang out
together outside of work?

985
00:44:01,300 --> 00:44:03,467
Yes, we go out together
sometimes.

986
00:44:03,467 --> 00:44:06,233
Because some groups
work really well together,

987
00:44:06,233 --> 00:44:10,000
but outside of work,
they don't actually get along.

988
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:12,367
They're not really friends.

989
00:44:12,367 --> 00:44:14,167
Well, we all have different
interests.

990
00:44:14,167 --> 00:44:16,933
For example, Juby and Jelai
always want to go shopping.

991
00:44:16,933 --> 00:44:19,167
They invite us,
but there's no pressure.

992
00:44:19,167 --> 00:44:20,567
Only those who want to join go.

993
00:44:20,567 --> 00:44:22,600
For example, Jo and I,
along with Arianne,

994
00:44:22,600 --> 00:44:24,367
love going on food trips,

995
00:44:24,367 --> 00:44:25,933
while Eriel and Ina

996
00:44:25,933 --> 00:44:27,333
- like playing games.
- We're homebodies.

997
00:44:27,333 --> 00:44:28,633
Homebodies
who like playing games.

998
00:44:28,633 --> 00:44:31,033
But it seems like you two
are the quietest in the group.

999
00:44:31,067 --> 00:44:32,333
Are you, or not?

1000
00:44:32,767 --> 00:44:34,800
We are.

1001
00:44:34,800 --> 00:44:37,433
Are you also the ones with
the worst breath in the group?

1002
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:39,867
Because you don't talk much. No?

1003
00:44:39,867 --> 00:44:43,233
We're not that quiet.

1004
00:44:43,233 --> 00:44:46,533
It's just that the other girls

1005
00:44:46,533 --> 00:44:48,600
have such strong and
loud personalities,

1006
00:44:48,600 --> 00:44:51,433
so the two of us tend
to let them take the lead.

1007
00:44:51,433 --> 00:44:54,067
"Fine, you guys do your thing."
Is that how it is?

1008
00:44:54,067 --> 00:44:55,567
But who's the kindest?

1009
00:44:55,567 --> 00:44:57,967
This is just based
on my observations,

1010
00:44:57,967 --> 00:45:00,733
since I don't really get to talk
to you all for long every day.

1011
00:45:00,733 --> 00:45:02,233
Just observing all of you.

1012
00:45:02,233 --> 00:45:04,900
I think Eriel is the kindest.

1013
00:45:04,933 --> 00:45:07,433
- [AUDIENCE SHOUTING]
- [VICE] No?

1014
00:45:07,433 --> 00:45:09,100
They disagree!

1015
00:45:09,100 --> 00:45:11,900
- [LAUGHTER]
- No! No!

1016
00:45:11,900 --> 00:45:15,233
The one who truly knows that
is the one you're always with.

1017
00:45:15,233 --> 00:45:18,667
Meme, we each have
our own quirks.

1018
00:45:18,667 --> 00:45:21,767
We have our own quirks.
That's why...

1019
00:45:21,767 --> 00:45:26,333
But Eriel is the most careful
with her words.

1020
00:45:26,333 --> 00:45:27,300
- [VICE] Oh.
- [CHOLE] There.

1021
00:45:27,300 --> 00:45:30,033
[JOHAIRA] And she's the type
to check on you.

1022
00:45:30,033 --> 00:45:31,533
- She shows respect.
- She's like that.

1023
00:45:31,533 --> 00:45:34,100
She's literally our youngest.

1024
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:36,767
Also, if you're an outsider,

1025
00:45:36,800 --> 00:45:39,567
you have an impression of
who's nice and who's not,

1026
00:45:39,567 --> 00:45:41,800
of who's kind and
who's the rule breaker.

1027
00:45:41,800 --> 00:45:44,867
But in reality, they're
all nice. Right?

1028
00:45:44,867 --> 00:45:47,067
They are just crazy
in their own ways.

1029
00:45:47,067 --> 00:45:48,500
It's the same for everyone.

1030
00:45:48,500 --> 00:45:50,500
You're nice and crazy
in your own way.

1031
00:45:50,500 --> 00:45:53,833
Is there a person who's
pure nice and no quirks?

1032
00:45:53,833 --> 00:45:55,667
That's not a person. That's AI.

1033
00:45:55,667 --> 00:45:57,633
- [LAUGHTER]
- Right?

1034
00:45:57,633 --> 00:45:58,833
There's nothing like that!

1035
00:45:58,833 --> 00:46:01,300
Your whole life
you're just nice?

1036
00:46:01,300 --> 00:46:03,133
You don't have any quirks?
That's not true.

1037
00:46:03,133 --> 00:46:05,567
All of us have a dark side.

1038
00:46:05,567 --> 00:46:09,600
We just have different ways
and time of showing it.

1039
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:11,367
What are your quirks in life?

1040
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:15,300
I love being alone.

1041
00:46:15,500 --> 00:46:17,667
- Ah.
- I'm really introverted.

1042
00:46:17,667 --> 00:46:18,833
- And then, I'm--
- You shouldn't have

1043
